+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Accuracy Sacrifice:** Setting fine-side vertex values based on the coarse-side interpolant ensures continuity but sacrifices some accuracy at the boundary [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Recursion Depth:** The recursive call for fine-side vertices must terminate. Since the shift moves the point to the coarser side, and the coarser side computes locally, recursion depth is limited by the refinement levels [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Epsilon Value:** The choice of $\epsilon$ must be small enough to not cross into another cell but large enough to avoid numerical precision issues [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Optimized Octant Generation](3412-optimized-octant-generation.md)
-An optimization for isosurface extraction on AMR data that reduces redundant computation by merging 'inner' octants into dual cells, while preserving crack-free continuity at level boundaries. It builds on the Octant Method by avoiding the recomputation of vertex values for shared inner octants, which the naïve approach computes eight times.
+An optimization for isosurface extraction on Adaptive Mesh Refinement (AMR) data that reduces redundant computation by merging 'inner' octants into dual cells, while preserving crack-free continuity at level boundaries. It builds on the [Octant Method](2648-octant-method.md) by avoiding the recomputation of vertex values for shared inner octants, which the naïve approach computes eight times.
